# Documentation voice

Storybook meta, **Pattern** stories, and agent notes describe **WMDS contracts only**.

## Do

- Document **props**, **anatomy**, **composition**, and **when to use** each component.
- Point to **Pattern — …** stories and **Best practices** for consuming apps and agents.
- Reference **ADRs** and **Foundations** token stories for architecture/token decisions.
- Use **For agents building UIs** on complex components when composition rules are easy to get wrong (see **Components/Data display/Avatar**).

## Don't

- Link or name external design systems in Storybook `docs.description` or component bullets in **AGENTS.md**.
- Write "inspired by …" or "maps X → Y" against another system's naming.
- Document raw Tailwind recipes as the primary API — **Pattern-first** (ADR-0004).

ADRs may record historical context; Storybook and **AGENTS.md** component bullets stay WMDS-native.
